{
  "id": "Compound::DB01189 - Gene::338567",
  "verbalization": "Desflurane is implicated in the pathogenic process through its ability to cause Breath Holding Attack, which is mediated by Isoflurane. Both Desflurane and Isoflurane share a common ancestor as Organofluorine Compounds and Anesthetic Agents, suggesting a shared pharmacological profile. The evidence indicates that Desflurane, through its role in inducing Breath Holding Attack, indirectly interacts with Kcnk18, as Isoflurane binds to this protein. This suggests a potential mechanism where Desflurane, via its interaction with Isoflurane, may influence Kcnk18 through the anesthetic pathway. The integration of these relationships highlights a possible dependency on anesthetic agents to modulate Kcnk18 activity, underscoring the role of anesthetic compounds in the pathophysiology of the observed effects.",
